{
  "$schema": "/scene-schema.json",
  "id": "js-event-loop",
  "title": "JavaScript Event Loop",
  "type": "concept",
  "layout": "code-left-canvas-right",
  "description": "See exactly how JavaScript handles async code — call stack, Web APIs, microtask queue, and callback queue all in one visual.",
  "category": "JavaScript",
  "code": {
    "language": "javascript",
    "source": "console.log('start');\n\nsetTimeout(() => {\n  console.log('setTimeout');\n}, 0);\n\nPromise.resolve()\n  .then(() => {\n    console.log('Promise');\n  });\n\nconsole.log('end');",
    "highlightByStep": [
      0,
      0,
      0,
      2,
      4,
      6,
      11,
      11,
      8,
      8,
      3,
      3
    ]
  },
  "canvas": [
    {
      "id": "call-stack",
      "type": "linear",
      "variant": "stack",
      "layoutHint": "linear-V",
      "label": "Call Stack",
      "initialState": {
        "items": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "microtask-queue",
      "type": "linear",
      "variant": "queue",
      "layoutHint": "linear-H",
      "label": "Microtask Queue",
      "initialState": {
        "items": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "callback-queue",
      "type": "linear",
      "variant": "queue",
      "layoutHint": "linear-H",
      "label": "Callback Queue (Macrotask)",
      "initialState": {
        "items": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "web-apis",
      "type": "system-diagram",
      "layoutHint": "dagre-LR",
      "label": "Web APIs",
      "initialState": {
        "components": [
          {
            "id": "web-api-box",
            "label": "Web APIs",
            "icon": "compute",
            "status": "normal"
          },
          {
            "id": "timer-box",
            "label": "Timer (0ms)",
            "icon": "compute",
            "status": "normal"
          }
        ],
        "connections": [
          {
            "id": "conn-webapi-timer",
            "from": "web-api-box",
            "to": "timer-box",
            "active": false
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "activeText": {
    "initialValue": "Script starts — call stack empty"
  },
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "snippet-toggle",
      "type": "toggle-group",
      "label": "Code Snippet",
      "config": {
        "options": [
          "setTimeout + Promise",
          "async/await",
          "Nested Microtasks"
        ],
        "defaultValue": "setTimeout + Promise"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "btn-run",
      "type": "button",
      "label": "Run Snippet",
      "config": {
        "variant": "primary",
        "defaultValue": null,
        "goToStep": 0
      }
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Synchronous Execution",
        "body": "`console.log('start')` is synchronous — it runs immediately when the engine reaches it.\n\nIt's pushed onto the call stack, executes, and is immediately popped."
      },
      "activeText": "console.log('start') → pushed to call stack",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "console.log('start')",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 2",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "console.log('start') executed → popped",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Web APIs Handle Async Work",
        "body": "`setTimeout` is not actually a JS feature — it's a **Web API** provided by the browser. When called, JS registers the callback with the browser and pops `setTimeout` off the stack immediately.\n\nJS doesn't wait — the browser handles the timer in the background.",
        "callout": "This is why setTimeout(fn, 0) doesn't mean \"run now\" — it means \"run after the current script finishes\"."
      },
      "activeText": "setTimeout(fn, 0) → pushed, then handed to Web APIs",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "setTimeout(fn, 0)",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "web-apis": {
          "componentStates": {
            "web-api-box": { "status": "active" },
            "timer-box": { "status": "active" }
          },
          "connectionStates": {
            "conn-webapi-timer": { "active": true }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 4",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "setTimeout registered → popped from stack",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Microtasks vs Macrotasks",
        "body": "There are **two** task queues:\n- **Microtask queue**: Promise callbacks, `queueMicrotask()` — runs after every task, before the browser paints\n- **Callback queue (macrotask)**: `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, I/O events — runs one per event loop tick\n\nThe event loop always **drains all microtasks before taking one macrotask**.",
        "callout": "This is why Promise.then() always runs before setTimeout, even setTimeout(fn, 0)."
      },
      "activeText": "Promise.resolve().then(fn) → microtask queued immediately",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "Promise.resolve().then(fn)",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "microtask-queue": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "Promise callback",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 6",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "console.log('end') → pushed and executed",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "console.log('end')",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "The Event Loop Tick",
        "body": "When the call stack is empty, the event loop:\n1. Runs **all** microtasks (until the microtask queue is empty)\n2. Takes **one** macrotask from the callback queue\n3. Renders any UI updates (browser only)\n4. Repeats"
      },
      "activeText": "Call stack empty → event loop checks microtask queue FIRST",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": []
        },
        "web-apis": {
          "componentStates": {
            "web-api-box": { "status": "normal" },
            "timer-box": { "status": "normal" }
          },
          "connectionStates": {
            "conn-webapi-timer": { "active": false }
          }
        },
        "callback-queue": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "setTimeout callback",
              "highlight": "insert"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 8",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "Microtask runs first — Promise callback → call stack",
      "canvas": {
        "microtask-queue": {
          "items": []
        },
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "Promise callback",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 9",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "Promise callback completes → now check callback queue",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Step 10",
        "body": "State updated."
      },
      "activeText": "Macrotask: setTimeout callback → call stack",
      "canvas": {
        "callback-queue": {
          "items": []
        },
        "call-stack": {
          "items": [
            {
              "id": "item-0",
              "value": "setTimeout callback",
              "highlight": "active"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "explanation": {
        "heading": "Execution Order Confirmed",
        "body": "Our code outputs:\n```\nstart\nend\nPromise callback  ← microtask\nsetTimeout callback  ← macrotask\n```\nThis holds true regardless of how long the timer delay is — even 0ms."
      },
      "activeText": "Done! Order: 'start' → 'end' → Promise → setTimeout",
      "canvas": {
        "call-stack": {
          "items": []
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "popups": [
    {
      "id": "pop-start",
      "attachTo": "call-stack",
      "text": "Synchronous — runs immediately",
      "showAtStep": 1,
      "hideAtStep": 2,
      "style": "info"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-settimeout",
      "attachTo": "web-apis",
      "text": "Handed off to browser — JS continues",
      "showAtStep": 3,
      "hideAtStep": 5,
      "style": "info"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-microtask",
      "attachTo": "microtask-queue",
      "text": "Promise callbacks queue instantly",
      "showAtStep": 5,
      "hideAtStep": 7,
      "style": "warning"
    },
    {
      "id": "pop-order",
      "attachTo": "call-stack",
      "text": "Microtasks ALWAYS run before macrotasks!",
      "showAtStep": 8,
      "hideAtStep": 10,
      "style": "insight"
    }
  ],
  "challenges": [
    {
      "id": "ch-predict-order",
      "title": "Predict the Output",
      "description": "What does this code print? `console.log(1); setTimeout(() => console.log(2), 0); Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log(3)); console.log(4);`\n\nGuess before stepping through!",
      "type": "predict"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-nested-microtask",
      "title": "Nested Microtasks",
      "description": "What if a Promise callback itself queues another microtask? Does the event loop drain it before moving to the macrotask? Try: `Promise.resolve().then(() => { Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('nested')); });`",
      "type": "predict"
    },
    {
      "id": "ch-starvation",
      "title": "Starvation Scenario",
      "description": "If microtasks keep queuing more microtasks (infinite loop of Promises), the macrotask queue (setTimeout callbacks) never runs. How would you fix a real-world bug caused by this?",
      "type": "scenario"
    }
  ]
}
